# Planted bugs for the blocking design. Each one must make its property fail.
run fv-tlc TwoPhaseCommit.tla BlockOnCrash.cfg WitnessAllCommitted.cfg
properties AllOrNothing EventuallyDecided
file TwoPhaseCommit.tla

mutation a manager can abort on its own, no matter what the coordinator decided
detects AllOrNothing
-     /\ tmState = "aborted" /\ rmState[rm] \in {"working", "prepared"}
+     /\ rmState[rm] \in {"working", "prepared"}

mutation recovery stays possible but nothing ever requires it to happen
detects EventuallyDecided
- Work == (\E rm \in RM : Prepare(rm) \/ RMLearnCommit(rm) \/ RMLearnAbort(rm) \/ RMTimeoutAbort(rm))
-          \/ TMCommit \/ TMAbort \/ Recover
- Next == Work \/ Crash \/ Done
+ Work == (\E rm \in RM : Prepare(rm) \/ RMLearnCommit(rm) \/ RMLearnAbort(rm) \/ RMTimeoutAbort(rm))
+          \/ TMCommit \/ TMAbort
+ Next == Work \/ Crash \/ Recover \/ Done

harmless a comment on the abort action
- \* Source: coordinator.abort(), which the coordinator can choose at any
+ \* Source: coordinator.abort(). The coordinator can choose this at any
